{title: More than my Hometown}
{artist: Morgan Wallen}
{key: G}
{comment: Structure: I V C V C B C T}

{start_of_intro}
{c: Guitar mellow, bass quiet but normal, high hat on 2 and 4}
| G / / / | Am / / / | Em / / / | Cadd9 / / / |
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Girl, our mamas are best friends and so are we
The [Am]whole town's rooting for us like the home team
[Em]Most likely to settle down
Plant a few [Cadd9]roots real deep and let 'em grow
<<[G (DRUMS IN)]But we can't stop this real world from spinnin' us
Your [Am]bright lights called, I don't blame you for pickin' up
Your [Em]big dream bags are all packed up and ready to [Cadd9]go
But I just need you to know>>
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
<<That I love you [G]more than a California sunset
More than a [Am]beer when you ain't twenty-one yet
More than a [Em]Sunday morning Lord
Turnin' some poor lost souls [Cadd9]'round, and Hallelujah bound
Yeah, I love you [G]more than the feeling when the bass hits the hook
When the [Am]guy gets the girl at the end of the book
But, baby, [Em]this might be the last time I get to lay you [Cadd9]down
'Cause I can't love you more than my home[G]town>>
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_interlude}
| G / / / | G / / / | G / / / | G / / / |
{end_of_interlude}

{start_of_verse}
<<[G]I ain't the runaway kind, I can't change that
My [Am]heart's stuck in these streets like the train tracks
[Em]City sky ain't the same black
Ain't that a [Cadd9]map dot shame, man, to think that>>
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
<<I love you [G]more than a California sunset
More than a [Am]beer when you ain't twenty-one yet
More than a [Em]Sunday morning Lord
Turnin' some poor lost souls [Cadd9]'round, and Hallelujah bound
Yeah, I love you [G]more than the feeling when the bass hits the hook
When the [Am]guy gets the girl at the end of the book
But, baby, [Em]this might be the last time I get to lay you down
'Cause I can't love you more than my home[G]town>>
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_interlude}
| G / / / | G / / / |
{end_of_interlude}

{start_of_bridge}
{c: No drums, bass and guitar on 1 of each measure}
<<You got a [G]wild in your eyes that I just wasn't born with
I'm a [Am]same gas station cup of coffee in the mornin'
I need a [Em]house on the hill, girl, not in 'em
So hang onto these words [Cadd9] 'til them avenues help you forget 'em>>
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
{c: Guitar mellow, bass quiet but normal, kick on "and 1" / "and 3", high hat on 2 and 4}
'Cause I love you [G]more than a California sunset
I love you [Am]more in a twenty-dollar sundress
Hate that [Em]loaded down car you got your keys in
<<Girl, but I [Cadd9]hate even more that you're leavin'
'Cause I love you [G (DRUMS IN)]more than the feeling when the bass hits the hook
When the [Am]guy gets the girl at the end of the book
But that [Em]ain't you and me so I guess I'll see you a[Cadd9]round
'Cause I can't love you more than my home[G (DRUMS OUT)]town>>
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_tag}
